Because particles may enter and leave, the partition sum must include all particle numbers: $\Xi(T,\mu)
=\sum_{N=0}^{\infty}\;\sum_{\mathcal C_N}
\exp\!\left[-\beta E(\mathcal C_N)+\beta\mu N\right].$ The inner sum runs over configurations with a specified $N$; the outer sum runs over $N$ itself. The grand-canonical weight may also be written $e^{-\beta(E-\mu N)}$.

