Keep the lattice but reinterpret its two states. Define an occupation number $n_i=\frac{1+\sigma_i}{2}
=
\begin{cases}
0,&\sigma_i=-1,\\
1,&\sigma_i=+1.
\end{cases}$ An empty site has spin down; an occupied site has spin up. Because $n_i$ can only be zero or one, double occupancy is forbidden. The lattice itself therefore supplies the hard core.

